# Forked from Alpine to run WebKitGTK 2.52.x while Alpine edge still ships
# 2.48.1. What 2.50->2.52 buys on a phone, measured missing on taimen
# 2026-09-01 (perceived scroll jank + video-content pacing behind a
# rock-steady 60 Hz compositor, brain finding
# waylandsink-5fps-was-two-upstream-policies-colliding and its overturn):
#
#   - damage propagation to the system compositor ENABLED (added in 2.48 but
#     default-off there; the compositor composites only what changed)
#   - thread-safe Skia recording (SkPictureRecorder) -- the 2.48 threaded
#     rendering was not thread-safe and caused rendering issues in release
#     builds
#   - main/scrolling/compositing thread synchronisation fixes (2.52/2.53
#     cycle) -- the named upstream fix for scroll glitches
#   - Managed MediaSource enabled for constrained devices (YouTube)
#
# The 2.48 fork's V4L2 sandbox patch is DROPPED: upstream bindV4l() now
# enumerates /dev and binds every videoN/mediaN/v4l-subdevN node, which is
# exactly what the patch did (Venus sits at /dev/video7 behind six camss
# nodes on msm8998). Verify with: grep -A8 "bindV4l" \
#   Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
#
# WHY pkgrel IS 50: apk installs the highest version it can see regardless
# of repo, so a local build at -r3 loses to a stock -r4 silently. A high
# pkgrel keeps this build winning for the life of the pkgver; an upstream
# 2.54.0 outranks it by design.
#
# Drop this fork when Alpine edge reaches 2.52.
#
# cull-tiles-outside-damage.patch stops CoordinatedBackingStore drawing tiles
# that cannot be visible. paintToTextureMapper() iterates every tile and calls
# drawTexture() on each; the only damage-aware path requires
# allEdgesExposed == No, so it helps EDGE tiles only and every interior tile of
# a page-sized layer is redrawn in full every frame. Measured on m.youtube.com
# (msm8998/A540): 73 quads, 61 Mpx drawn for a 3.7 Mpx viewport, 33 of them
# full-width tiles from three page-sized layers.
#
# Safe because TextureMapper is handed AcceleratedSurface::renderTargetDamage()
# -- the damage accumulated since THAT render target was last drawn into -- so
# content outside it is already present in the buffer even though the swap
# chain hands out a different one each frame (ThreadedCompositor.cpp, the
# setDamage() call under DamagePropagationFlags::UseForCompositing).
#
# It therefore only does anything with damage-clip-compositing-on-gtk.patch
# also applied: without UseForCompositing, textureMapper.damage() is null and
# no culling is possible at all. That flip is the prerequisite; this is where
# the GPU work actually comes off.
#
#
# cull-tiles-outside-clip.patch is the same idea against the scissor box rather
# than the damage, and it is the half that helps SCROLLING: while scrolling the
# damage is the whole viewport, so the damage cull cannot fire, but most tiles
# of a page-sized layer are still off screen. drawTexture() only early-outs
# when the scissor box is EMPTY, so a tile that simply misses the box still
# issues its draw call, uniforms and vertices -- and a tiling GPU visits every
# draw once per bin it might touch. Unlike the damage cull this needs no damage
# tracking and no preference flip.
#
# Why this rather than pipelining the compositor: the frame period is cpu paint
# plus the GPU tail, serialized, and pinning the GPU to its lowest OPP took the
# compositor period from 32.9 to 53.5 ms, so the GPU half is real work rather
# than idle waiting. Cutting that work also cuts heat, where overlapping it
# would raise it.
#
#
# damage-clip-compositing-on-gtk.patch flips two GTK preference defaults so
# WebKit clips its OWN compositing to the rectangles it damaged:
#
#   UseDamagingInformationForCompositing  false -> true   (was off everywhere)
#   UnifyDamagedRegions                   true  -> false  (was GTK-only true)
#
# Upstream collects damage on GTK and forwards a tight rect to the system
# compositor, but never uses it internally, and Unify collapses the frame's
# damage to one bounding box. TextureMapperLayer::collectDamageSelf() marks any
# layer with a contents buffer -- the decoded video layer -- fully damaged every
# frame, so the bounding box IS the viewport and Epiphany recomposites all of it
# for a playing video. Flipping only the first pref is measurably neutral for
# exactly that reason; both are needed.
#
# Measured on taimen (msm8998/A540) 2026-09-04, MiniBrowser --features A/B on
# 4K60 YouTube, 60 s: compositor commit p50 38.7 -> 35.7 ms, p90 44.6 -> 41.3,
# worst frame 162 -> 112 ms, die at saturation 80.3 -> 77.5 C. WEBKIT_SHOW_DAMAGE
# shows the whole viewport tinted before and discrete rectangles after.
# Rectangles mode does NOT flood the system compositor: the wayland log shows
# exactly one wl_surface.damage_buffer per commit in both arms.
#
# dont-relayout-fixed-objects-on-async-scroll.patch,
# no-fake-mouse-moves-for-touch-scrolling.patch and
# video-flush-keeps-the-last-frame.patch are the 2026-09-06 scroll/video
# campaign. Each carries its own measured rationale in its header; in short:
#   * LocalFrameView::updateLayoutViewport() calls setNeedsLayout() on every
#     fixed/sticky renderer on every scroll even when the scrolling thread owns
#     those layers -- 540 times per 12 s drag, and a fixed element's containing
#     block is the RenderView, so it dirties the root.
#   * every scroll arms a fake mousemove; on a touch-only device it fires at each
#     drag stop and costs a forced layout plus a hover restyle (73 calls, 437 ms
#     per drag) to update :hover for a pointer that does not exist.
#   * a GStreamer flush nulls the video layer on any hardware-buffer path
#     (DMABuf / external-OES / YUV), so every YouTube quality switch blanks the
#     video until the next decoded frame -- the "quick flash" on 4K60.
#
# shareable-bitmap-null-surface.patch (r62) and
# composite-css-filters-on-coordinated-graphics.patch (r63), 2026-09-06:
#   * Epiphany asks for a FULL_DOCUMENT snapshot for its overview thumbnail;
#     a long article is 2802x237522 px = 2.66 GB, Skia refuses a raster surface
#     over 2 GB and ShareableBitmap::createGraphicsContext() dereferenced the
#     null. Upstream main has the same bug. (temp/epiphany stops asking.)
#   * the GTK port never composites a layer for its CSS filter alone, so
#     YouTube's ambient-mode blur(40px) was rasterised by Skia on the CPU on
#     the web process main thread, 1.4-3.2 s per repaint every 7-12 s -- the
#     multi-second video freezes. FilterTrigger on Coordinated Graphics, gated
#     to filters that move pixels so 40 brightness() thumbnails do not each
#     cost an intermediate surface per frame (measured: 34 -> 45 ms p50).
#
# lead-the-prepaint-in-the-scroll-direction.patch, 2026-09-09. The backing
# store prepaints (multiplier - 1) x viewport height of tiles, and upstream
# splits that budget EQUALLY above and below the visible rect. During a fling
# only the leading half is ever shown; the trailing half is content the user
# has already passed. This adds WEBKIT_LAYERS_COVER_LEAD, the share of the
# vertical budget to put ahead, defaulting to 0.5 -- which is upstream's split
# exactly, so it lands as a no-op and is A/B'd at runtime.
#
# WHY IT IS WORTH HAVING. Measured on taimen 2026-09-09, one 6-fling drag:
# raising the multiplier from 2 to 4 removed every frame that was more than
# half unpainted, and cost 740 -> 1415 MB of tile memory against a scope capped
# at 1500M. Moving the SAME budget forward is the cheap half of that. The block
# it has to bridge is CoordinatedPlatformLayer::record on the main thread: on
# the YouTube watch page that is 2954 ms of an 11.4 s drag window, p90 135 ms,
# max 200 ms, and the compositor keeps scrolling at 60 Hz through all of it.
#
# IT IS A TRADE. The trailing prepaint is what makes an immediate reversal
# cheap, so a lead near 1.0 buys a smooth fling and pays for it the moment the
# user flings back.
#
# AND IT MEASURED NULL, so it stays off. Three arms a side on a 79000 px
# Wikipedia article, 0.5 (= upstream) against 0.85:
#
#   lead   blank band >40% of the viewport   client worst frame   jank>33ms
#   0.5              0, 2, 2                  93, 215, 182 ms      11, 26, 25
#   0.85             3, 2, 2                  133, 236, 72 ms      19, 28, 15
#
# Means 20.7 janks either way, and the band metric saturates at 1.0 in five of
# the six arms, so a partial improvement could hide inside it. Read it as "no
# effect this arm can see", not as proof of zero.
#
# WHY, most likely: the block that has to be bridged is ~200 ms of record on
# the main thread, and a fling covers more than the WHOLE prepaint budget in
# that time -- so what is needed is more budget, not better-placed budget.
# Raising WEBKIT_LAYERS_COVER_MULTIPLIER to 4 does remove the worst frames and
# costs 740 -> 1415 MB of tile memory, which is why it is not the answer either.
pkgname=webkit2gtk-6.0
pkgver=2.52.6
pkgrel=64
pkgdesc="Portable web rendering engine WebKit for GTK+ - GTK4 version"
url="https://webkitgtk.org/"
arch="all"
license="LGPL-2.0-or-later AND BSD-2-Clause"
depends="bubblewrap xdg-dbus-proxy dbus:org.freedesktop.Secrets"
# bubblewrap and xdg-dbus-proxy are runtime depends that cmake also needs to
# find as EXECUTABLES at configure time (BubblewrapSandboxChecks.cmake). Alpine
# gets away with listing them only in depends= because abuild installs $depends
# into the buildroot too; pmbootstrap resolves dependencies itself and installs
# makedepends only, so configure dies with "xdg-dbus-proxy executable not found
# and is needed for ENABLE_BUBBLEWRAP_SANDBOX" after ~90s. List them here too.
#
# libjxl-dev is listed statically below as well as in the case $CARCH block
# further down. pmbootstrap cannot see the conditional one: pmb/parse/_apkbuild.py
# reads APKBUILDs line by line and never executes the shell, so a makedepends
# appended inside a case statement is invisible and the package never lands in
# the buildroot. The build then dies in cmake with "libjxl is required for
# USE_JPEGXL" after ~90s of configure, which reads like a missing distro package
# rather than a parser limitation.
makedepends="
	libjxl-dev
	bubblewrap
	xdg-dbus-proxy
	bison
	clang
	cmake
	enchant2-dev
	flex
	flite-dev
	geoclue-dev
	gnutls-dev
	gobject-introspection-dev
	gperf
	gst-plugins-bad-dev
	gst-plugins-base-dev
	gstreamer-dev
	gtk4.0-dev
	hyphen-dev
	icu-dev
	lcms2-dev
	libavif-dev
	libgcrypt-dev
	libjpeg-turbo-dev
	libmanette-dev
	libpng-dev
	libseccomp-dev
	libsecret-dev
	libsoup3-dev
	libwebp-dev
	libwpe-dev
	libwpebackend-fdo-dev
	libxcomposite-dev
	libxml2-dev
	libxslt-dev
	libxt-dev
	lld
	llvm
	mesa-dev
	openjpeg-dev
	pango-dev
	python3
	ruby
	ruby-getoptlong
	samurai
	sqlite-dev
	sysprof-dev
	sysprof-static
	unifdef
	woff2-dev
	"
options="!check" # upstream doesn't package them in release tarballs: Tools/Scripts/run-gtk-tests: Command not found
subpackages="$pkgname-dbg $pkgname-lang $pkgname-dev"
source="https://webkitgtk.org/releases/webkitgtk-$pkgver.tar.xz
	cloopfix.patch
	riscv64-no-wasm.patch
	loongarch64-fix-simde.patch
	x11-include-order.patch
	frame-done-at-fence.patch
	keep-fbo-across-texture-reset.patch
	skip-empty-tiles.patch
	damage-clip-compositing-on-gtk.patch
	cull-tiles-outside-damage.patch
	cull-tiles-outside-clip.patch
	pipeline-compositor-frames-in-flight.patch
	cull-quads-outside-the-scissor-box.patch
	split-oversized-recordings-and-cap-prepaint.patch
	dont-relayout-fixed-objects-on-async-scroll.patch
	no-fake-mouse-moves-for-touch-scrolling.patch
	video-flush-keeps-the-last-frame.patch
	shareable-bitmap-null-surface.patch
	composite-css-filters-on-coordinated-graphics.patch
	lead-the-prepaint-in-the-scroll-direction.patch
	"
builddir="$srcdir/webkitgtk-$pkgver"

case "$CARCH" in
s390x) ;;
*)
	makedepends="$makedepends libjxl-dev"
	;;
esac

# secfixes:
#   2.36.5-r0:
#     - CVE-2022-2294
#     - CVE-2022-32792
#     - CVE-2022-32816
#   2.36.4-r0:
#     - CVE-2022-22677
#     - CVE-2022-22710

build() {
	case "$CARCH" in
	arm*|aarch64|s390x|riscv64|x86)
		# lto broken on these arches
		;;
	*)
		local lto="-DLTO_MODE=thin"
		;;
	esac

	case "$CARCH" in
	s390x)
		# no libjxl
		local jxl="-DUSE_JPEGXL=OFF"
		;;
	esac

	case "$CARCH" in
	riscv64)
		# not supported
		local jit="
			-DENABLE_JIT=OFF
			-DENABLE_C_LOOP=ON
			-DENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY=OFF
		"
		;;
	esac

	case "$CARCH" in
	armv7)
		# https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/132322
		# https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=290167
		;;
	*)
		# the debug symbols become 1/2 the size, and actual webkit becomes
		# smaller too.
		export CC=clang
		export CXX=clang++
		export LDFLAGS="$LDFLAGS -fuse-ld=lld"
		;;
	esac

	export AR=llvm-ar
	export NM=llvm-nm
	export RANLIB=llvm-ranlib

	# significantly reduce debug symbol size
	export CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -g1"
	export CXXFLAGS="$CXXFLAGS -g1"

	# broken with fortify
	export CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -U_FORTIFY_SOURCE"
	export CXXFLAGS="$CXXFLAGS -U_FORTIFY_SOURCE"

	cmake -B build -G Ninja \
		-DPORT=GTK \
		-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
		-DCMAKE_SKIP_RPATH=ON \
		-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr \
		-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \
		-DENABLE_DOCUMENTATION=OFF \
		-DENABLE_JOURNALD_LOG=OFF \
		-DENABLE_MINIBROWSER=ON \
		-DENABLE_SAMPLING_PROFILER=OFF \
		-DENABLE_SPELLCHECK=ON \
		-DENABLE_SPEECH_SYNTHESIS=ON \
		-DUSE_GTK4=ON \
		-DUSE_LIBBACKTRACE=OFF \
		$lto \
		$jxl \
		$jit
	cmake --build build
}

check() {
	ninja -C build check
}

package() {
	DESTDIR="$pkgdir" cmake --install build
	mv "$pkgdir"/usr/bin/WebKitWebDriver "$pkgdir"/usr/bin/WebKitWebDriver-6.0
}

